WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.350
Act 1.

2
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:05.460
A young man, alone, prays: "Thou, Nature,

3
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:11.710
art my goddess;" Soon after, an old
king raises his hands to the same sky:

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.750
"Hear, nature, hear; dear goddess, hear!"

5
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.130
Two prayers to one goddess.

6
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.820
But what does each man
see when he looks up?

7
00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.110
Same goddess, same word.

8
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.070
So do they mean the same thing?

9
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.810
In this mission, you'll learn what the
word nature could mean in Shakespeare's

10
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.590
time, and test each man against it.

11
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.270
You'll hear the old king turn that
goddess against his own daughter,

12
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.110
in a furious curse.

13
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.830
And you'll see why a king splitting
Britain with a map mattered,

14
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.680
after James I united the crowns in 1603.

15
00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:48.130
Your mission: decide whether
they mean the same thing.
